囲碁 — position reading tests
eyes — 眼
  ok    corner eye
  ok    not an eye for the other colour
  ok    corner with an enemy diagonal is not an eye
  ok    centre eye
  ok    centre eye survives one enemy diagonal
  ok    two enemy diagonals — false eye
  ok    an open side is not an eye
  ok    an occupied point is not an eye
useful moves — 有用手
  ok    every point is useful on an empty board
  ok    an empty board is not a dead end
  ok    black will not fill its own eyes
  ok    black has nothing left to play
  ok    white cannot play there either — suicide
a real game — 129 moves, White to move
  ok    white group is 13 stones
  ok    with exactly one liberty
  ok    G5 is White's only eye
  ok    White has no useful move
  ok    White is at a dead end
  ok    Black still has moves
move selection — 着手選択
  ok    takes the free capture
  ok    the chain really is in atari
  ok    escapes through its only liberty
  ok    passes rather than fill its own eyes
  ok    opens in a corner, every time
  ok    its move on a crowded board is legal
self-play — the engine against itself
  ok    never proposes an illegal move
  ok    the game actually progressed
  ok    and put stones on the board
invasion guard — 侵入の見張り
  ok    a move deep in enemy territory scores below zero
  ok    an ordinary point far from the wall is not penalised
  ok    touching two enemy stones is not a tactical excuse
  ok    the guard is not applied at beginner level
  ok    the same holds for White inside Black's wall
  ok    the white stone really is in atari
  ok    a capture is worth playing however deep it is
hunting — 追討
  ok    the invader really has four liberties
  ok    approaching it beats playing far from it in the same area
  ok    both chains are down to two liberties
  ok    the big chain is three stones
  ok    threatening three stones beats threatening one
  ok    the stone to be taken has one liberty
  ok    the other one still has two
  ok    capturing outscores merely closing in
defence — 守り
  ok    the friendly chain is down to two liberties
  ok    giving it another liberty beats playing elsewhere
PASS — the engine reads the position
